see "../src/harness.vox".
see "../src/runner.vox".
see "../src/rng.vox".
see "../src/gen_literals.vox".
see "../src/gen_manifest.vox".
see "../src/gen_core.vox".
see "../src/gen_buffers.vox".
see "../src/gen_files.vox".
see "../src/gen_collections.vox".
see "../src/gen_text.vox".
see "../src/gen_things.vox".
see "../src/gen_flow.vox".
see "../src/gen_misc.vox".

(Ledger batch VAL-B: the seven `value` leaves (docs/ledger/values.md rows
 VAL-02, 04, 12, 14, 21, 25, 27).

 Same shape as 270_gen_values_a and for the same reason: the emitted text
 is COMPILED AND RUN by the real compiler, because the only thing these
 leaves exist for is that their assertions hold, and reading the text
 alone would miss it. The program ends `Exit 0.`, so any other status is
 either a ledger assertion that fired (95) or a crash.

 Emitted twice from one seed and compared, because these leaves spend
 names out of the shared vocabulary the batch-A leaves spend from: if
 that record ever outlived a program, two programs from one seed would
 stop being identical and every campaign's reproducibility would go with
 them.)

To 'emit the absent and forms leaves'.
    clear gen_out.
    'gen reset value names'.
    'gen leaf value forms' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf value dispatch label' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf value retype tracking' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf value type property' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf absent value' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf absent test' of "" and false.
    'gen leaf absent key' of "" and false.
    'gen emit' of "Exit 0.\n".

'rng seed' of 11.
'emit the absent and forms leaves'.
a text called 'the first emission' is 'gen text'.
'gen write' of "./vf_values_b.vox".

'rng seed' of 11.
'emit the absent and forms leaves'.
a text called 'the second emission' is 'gen text'.
Print "reproducible: {'the first emission' is equal to 'the second emission'}".

a boolean called 'the forms row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-02".
Print "VAL-02 asserts: {'the forms row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the dispatch row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-04".
Print "VAL-04 asserts: {'the dispatch row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the tracking row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-12".
Print "VAL-12 asserts: {'the tracking row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the type property row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-14".
Print "VAL-14 asserts: {'the type property row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the absent value row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-21".
Print "VAL-21 asserts: {'the absent value row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the absent test row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-25".
Print "VAL-25 asserts: {'the absent test row is covered'}".
a boolean called 'the absent key row is covered' is 'gen text contains' of "ASSERT VAL-27".
Print "VAL-27 asserts: {'the absent key row is covered'}".

(The constructs these seven rows turn on, checked by needle rather than
 by leaf name: the `type` property read on a value, an `is nothing` test
 and its negation, and the retype statement.)
a boolean called 'the type property appears' is 'gen text contains' of "s type is not \"".
Print "the type property emitted: {'the type property appears'}".
a boolean called 'an absent test appears' is 'gen text contains' of "is nothing then,".
Print "is nothing emitted: {'an absent test appears'}".
a boolean called 'a present test appears' is 'gen text contains' of "is not nothing then,".
Print "is not nothing emitted: {'a present test appears'}".
a boolean called 'a drained handler appears' is 'gen text contains' of "On error Set ".
Print "a drained handler emitted: {'a drained handler appears'}".

(The compiler comes from 'vox path', which honours $VOX the way test.sh
 sets it - a literal ../vox/... would only be right in a plain checkout
 and would silently skip the check in a worktree.)
a text called 'the compile command' is "{'shell quote' of 'vox path'} ./vf_values_b.vox -o ./vf_values_b > ./vf_values_b.cerr 2>&1".
a number called 'the compile status' is 'run shell' of 'the compile command' and 60000.
Print "the value leaves compile: {'the compile status' is 0}".
a number called 'the run status' is 'run shell' of "./vf_values_b > ./vf_values_b.out 2>&1" and 60000.
Print "every value assertion holds: {'the run status' is 0}".

(Only on failure, so the expected file is unchanged when this passes.)
If 'the compile status' is not 0 then,
    a text called 'the compiler complaint' is 'read whole file' of "./vf_values_b.cerr",
    Print "the compiler was {'vox path'}",
    Print 'the compiler complaint'.
If 'the run status' is not 0 then,
    a text called 'what the program printed' is 'read whole file' of "./vf_values_b.out",
    Print 'what the program printed'.
